   "evidence": "Line 44: `/-- The integral Cartan matrix, specialized to the coefficient ring. -/ abbrev matrix : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) R := !![0, -1; 1, -1]`. The module docstring itself describes this matrix as an action on the Cartan part of a root-free datum, not as a Cartan matrix.",
   "file": "TauCeti/LinearAlgebra/FixedSubmodule/OrderThree.lean",
   "fix": "Reword, e.g. \"The matrix `[[0,-1],[1,-1]]` of the order-three automorphism of the rank-two cocharacter lattice, with entries in `R`.\"",
   "issue": "The docstring \"The integral Cartan matrix, specialized to the coefficient ring\" calls `!![0, -1; 1, -1]` a Cartan matrix. That standard Lie-theory term means the root/coroot pairing matrix (for A\u2082, [[2,-1],[-1,2]]), but this matrix is an order-three automorphism of the cocharacter lattice, and its entries lie in an arbitrary ring `R`, not \u2124.",
   "line": 44
  }
